$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Experimental Procedure of Compound 3a
NaI (0.149 mg, 1 mmol) and TMSCl (0.127 ml, 1 mmol) were added to a
solution of the aldehyde 1 (106 mg, 1 mmol) in CH2Cl2 and the mixture was
stirred for 10 min. Then the reaction mixture was brought to -78 °C and a
solution of 2-(trimethylsilyloxy)furan 2 (1 mmol) in CH2Cl2 was added
dropwise. The reaction mixture was stirred at -78 °C until the reaction
was completed as indicated by thin-layer chromatography (TLC). The
reaction mixture was washed with Na2S2O3, followed by brine, dried on
Na2SO4, concentrated under reduced pressure and purified by silicagel
column chromatography to get the pure product 3a. Compound 3a (Threo
isomer). White solid. Compound 3a (Erythro isomer). White solid. Entry 1
product 3a/4a. Table 1. Reactions of various aldehydes with
2-(trimethylsilyloxy)furan Entry 2. Product 3b/4b. Yield 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM TMSI-promoted diastereoselective synthesis of
5-(1'-hydroxy)-γ-butyrolactones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sabitha, Gowravaram; Prasad, M. Nagendra; Yadav, J. S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2011), 41(15), 2290-2295

