$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.2. Diastereoselective Mukaiyama aldol
reaction of cyclohexanones with acyclic ketene acetals Ethyl
(1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)cyclohexyl)acetate (4a) Ethyl
2-((1R*,2S*)-1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2-methylcyclohexyl)-2-methylpropanoate
(4f) According to the synthetic procedure for 4a, this compound was
obtained in 90% yield (308.4 mg, 0.90 mmol) by the reaction of
2-methylcyclohexanone 2b (121 μL, 1.0 mmol) with
tert-butyl(1-ethoxy-2-methylpropenyloxy)-dimethylsilane (346.0 mg, 1.5
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) in the presence of Tf2CHCH2CHTf2 1 (5.7 mg, 10
μmol) for 2.5 h at -178 °C. Colorless oil. IR (neat) ν 2954, 2933, 2857,
1724, 1253, 1122, 1064, 1051, 833, 771 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
0.19 (6H, s), 0.96 (9H, s), 0.99 (3H, dd, J = 6.3 Hz), 1.11-1.32 (2H, m),
1.258 (3H, t, J = 7.3 Hz), 1.264 (3H, s), 1.29 (3H, s), 1.43-1.73 (7H,
m), 4.02-4.11 (1H, m), 4.12-4.21 (1H, m); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
-11.4 and -11.3, 14.1, 18.6, 20.2, 21.9, 23.6 and 23.8, 25.4, 26.8, 32.5,
33.6, 39.3, 52.7, 60.2, 81.4, 177.3; MS (ESI-TOF) m/z 343 [M+ H]+; HRMS
calcd for C19H39O3Si [M+ H]+, 343.2668; found, 343.2686. Anal. Calcd for
C19H38O3Si: C, 66.61; H, 11.18. Found: C, 66.55; H, 11.06.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
