$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction Profile of the Catalytic Aldol Addition of 3b to Pivalaldehyde.
The reaction of 3b and pivalaldehyde was performed on a 20 mmol scale at
-78 °C in dichloromethane (40 mL) under the influence of 3 mol% of the
catalyst. Small quantities of the solution sampled from the reaction
vessel were rapidly quenched by pyridine at -78°C to avoid desilylation
of the adduct. The chemical yields were estimated by GLC analysis using
the produced 4-bromo-2,6-di-tert-butylphenol as an internal standard
(time program: from 70 °C to 230 °C at a rate of 5 °C/min). GLC retention
times: anti aldol adduct: t R = 9.02 min, syn aldol adduct: t R = 10.68
min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, MABR co-catalyst prepared and
used, syn/anti ratio =15:85
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Remarkable Enhancement of Catalyst Activity of Trialkylsilyl Sulfonates
on the Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction: A New Approach Using Bulky
Organoaluminum Cocatalysts
