$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the Catalytic
Asymmetric Vinylogous Mukaiyama Aldol Addition: Preparation of
(E)-(R)-5-hydroxy-2-methyl-dec-2- enethioic acid S-tert-butyl ester SI7.
The crude reaction mixture was obtained by following the general
procedure for the catalytic asymmetric vinylogous Mukaiyama aldol
addition using hexanal (90.0 μL, 0.745 mmol, 1.00 eq) as starting
material and was purified by flash chromatography using a 2.5 × 18 cm
silica gel column eluting with a solvent mixture of 5% acetone/hexanes
(600 mL). The eluant was collected in 30 mL portions and the product
containing fractions (6 to 22) were combined and concentrated to give
alcohol SI7 (182 mg, 0.668 mmol, 90%) as a clear colorless oil. The ratio
of enantiomers was determined to be er = 95:5 (with BF3•EtO2 as
Lewis-acid, er = 51:49) by HPLC analysis using a Daicel Chiralcel OD-H
silica column, eluting with a mobile phase of 2.5% 2-propanol/hexanes and
a flow rate of 0.5 mL/min, which gave the retention times for the major
and minor enantiomers of 14.5 and 15.7 min, respectively, detecting with
a Rainin Dynamax Refractive Index Detector Model RI-1: Rf 0.55 (20%
acetone/hexanes); [α]D 20 -6.7 (c = 1.090, CHCl3); 500 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3)
δ 6.73 (dd, J = 7.3, 7.3 Hz, 1H), 3.77 (dddd, J = 6.9, 5.6, 5.4, 5.1 Hz,
1H), 2.40 – 2.30 (m, 2H), 1.86 (s, 3H), 1.60 (bs, 1H), 1.51 – 1.47 (m,
2H), 1.49 (s, 9H), 1.35 – 1.29 (m, 6H), 0.91 – 0.89(m, 3H); 125 MHz 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ 195.0, 139.1, 135.7, 71.3, 47.7, 37.4, 36.9, 32.0, 30.1
(3), 25.6, 22.8, 14.2, 12.8; 125 MHz DEPT (CDCl3) δ CH3: 30.1 (3), 14.2,
12.8. CH2: 37.4, 36.9, 32.0, 25.6, 22.8. CH: 135.7, 71.3. C: 195.0,
139.1, 47.7; IR (neat) 3424 (bs), 2956, 2928, 2863, 1721, 1651, 1456,
1388, 1380, 1363, 1264, 1220, 1162, 1127, 1075, 1027, 1011, 985, 931,
898, 840, 727, 693, 659 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C15H28O2S: C, 66.13; H,
10.36. Found: C, 66.15; H, 10.43.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 4A mol. sieves used
