$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method A; To a solution of isatin (271 mg, 1.84 mmol) in dry
dichloromethane (55 mL) under argon atmosphere was carefully dropped
titanium tetrachloride (0.60 mL, 1.0 M in dichloromethane) at -78 °C,
then the color was turned yellow. After stirring for 30 min, the solution
of vinylketene N,O-acetal (100 mg, 0.3 mmol) in dry dichloromethane (5
mL) was added dropwise. After stirring for 6 hr, to the reaction mixture
was pyridine (0.20 mL). The resulting mixture was poured to the mixture
of a saturated aqueous solution of (+/-)-sodium potassium tartrate and a
saturated aqueous solution of sodium bicarbonate (1 : 1) at 0 °C. After
the organic layer was clear, aqueous layer was extracted with
dichloromethane. The combined extracts were washed with brine, dried over
anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified via column chromatography (Hexane / Chloroform /
Ethyl acetate = 3 / 1 / 1) to afford alcohol, yield 99 mg, 90% as a 31 :
1 diastereomeric mixture. Information not present.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative prepn. shown
