$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Hydroxymethylation of the silyl enol ether of propiophenone with a
formaldehyde water solution. To a suspension of PMI Sc(OTf)3 (109 mg,
0.020 mmol, 5 mol%) in CH3CN (1.85 mL) were added a 37% formaldehyde
water solution (150 μL, 201 mmol) and the silyl enol ether of propiophene
(84 mg, 0.41 mmol) at room temperature. The mixture was stirred for 0.5 h
at room temperature. After filtration and washing (CH2Cl2, hexane), the
filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure, and the resulting crude
compound was purified by PTLC to give
3-hydroxy-2-methyl-1-phenylpropane-1-onemethyl14 (60 mg, 90%). Colorless
oil; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ = 1.25 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 2.29 (br s, 1H), 3.67
(m, 1H), 3.83 (m, 1H), 3.93 (m, 1H), 7.46–7.61 (m, 3H), 7.95–7.98 (m,
2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ = 14.5, 42.9, 64.5, 128.4, 128.7, 133.3, 136.1,
204.4. In this reaction, Sc leaching (41%) was observed by XRF analysis.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Polymer-Micelle Incarcerated Scandium as a Polymer-Supported Catalyst for
High-Throughput Organic Synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Takeuchi, Masahiro; Akiyama, Ryo; Kobayashi, Shu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2005), 127(38), 13096-13097

