$DATUM 1-{6-[2-(tert-Butyldimethylsilanyloxy)ethyl]-5-methyltetrahydropyran-
2-yl}-6-methylhept-3-yn-2-one (28). To a solution of the freshly prepared
silyl enol ether 27 (4.66 g, 23.8 mmol, 2 equiv) and freshly prepared
acetate 25 (3.76 g, 11.9 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (160 mL) at -78 °C
was added a solution of ZnCl2 (26.2 mL, 1.0 M in Et2O, 26.18 mmol, 2.2
equiv). The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to rt, quenched by
addition of a saturated solution of NaHCO3, and diluted with Et2O. The
aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O, and the combined organic extracts
were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated. The
residue was purified by silica gel chromatography (petroleum ether/Et2O
95:5 to 90:10) to afford the trans-tetrahydropyran 28 (4.03 g,
89%)-(trans/cis THP 13:1 by GC): [α]D 20 +44.9 (c 0.92, CHCl3); IR (neat)
3000-2800, 2210, 1673, 1462, 1251, 1165, 1083 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ 4.60 (dddd, J = 7.7, 6.4, 5.0, 4.6 Hz, 1H), 3.70 (ddd, J = 10.0,
7.5, 5.1 Hz, 1H), 3.61 (m, 1H), 3.36 (ddd, J = 8.7, 7.3, 3.7 Hz, 1H),
2.90 (dd, J = 15.1, 7.7 Hz, 1H), 2.66 (dd, J = 15.1, 6.4 Hz, 1H), 2.26
(d, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H), 1.90 (m, J = 6.7 Hz, 1H), 1.82-1.64 (m, 4H),
1.54-1.28 (m, 3H), 1.01 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 6H), 0.93 (d, J = 6.7, 3H), 0.88
(s, 9H), 0.04 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 185.8 (s), 93.6 (s),
81.8 (s), 73.8 (d), 67.7 (d), 60.1 (t), 48.6 (t), 35.8 (t), 33.6 (d),
28.0 (t), 27.6 (d), 27.5 (t), 26.6 (t), 26.0 (q, 3C), 22.0 (q, 2C), 18.3
(s), 18.2 (q), -5.3 (2q); MS (EI), 323 (M - t-Bu+, 27), 293 (58), 199
(100), 175 (10), 143 (37), 139 (14), 131 (19), 109 (41), 107 (34), 99
(25), 81 (M - C7H9O, 15), 75 (48); HRMS (ESI) calcd for C22H40O3Si + Na+
403.2639, found 403.2640.
