$DATUM 4-[(1,1'-Dibenzyl-2-oxo-1,2-dihydro-1'H-[3,3']biindolyl-3-yl)hydroxymethyl]-2,2-
dimethyloxazolidine-3-carboxylic acid tert-butyl ester (9). To a cold
(-78 °C), stirring solution of (R)-Garner’s aldehyde 83 (2.30 g, 10.0
mmol), 2,6-di-tert-butyl-4-methylpyridine (7.3 mL, 30 mmol), and CH2Cl2
(75 mL) was added dropwise BF3·Et2O (6.8 mL, 54 mmol) via syringe. A
solution of freshly prepared silyloxy indole 7 (3.7 g, 6.8 mmol) and
CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was added dropwise. After stirring for 3 h at -78 °C, the
reaction mixture was allowed to warm to -50 °C where it was maintained
for 9 h. The reaction solution then was poured into saturated aqueous
ammonium chloride (50 mL), the phases were separated, and the aqueous
phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x50 mL). The combined organic layers
were washed sequentially with saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate and
brine, dried (MgSO4), and concentrated to afford a yellowish oil, which
HPLC analysis showed to be almost exclusively (>80:1) one
stereoisomer.Purification of this oil by column chromatography (3/1
hexanes/EtOAc) provided 9 (4.0 g, 89%) as a colorless solid: colorless
solid: mp 93-95°C; [α]23 D -22.5, [α]23 577 = -23.8, [α]23 546 = -28.7 (c
= 1.45, CHCl3); UV (CH2Cl2) 253 nm (19700), 287 nm (15500); IR (film)
3471, 3064, 2979, 1686, 1611 cm-1; HRMS (CI) calcd for C41H43N3O5Na
(M+Na): 680.3101; found: 680.3090.4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Construction of Quaternary Carbon Stereocenters: High
Stereoselection in Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions of 2-Siloxyindoles with
Chiral Aldehydes
