$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Desilylation of
Mukaiyama Aldol Compounds. To a mixture of 10 (without purification, 1.0
mmol) in MeOH (5 mL) and THF (2-5 mL) was added 12% HCl(aq) (2.1 mL, 7
mmol), and then the resulting mixture was stirred for an additional 6 h
at 30 °C. After evaporation of most of the MeOH and THF, the resulting
residue was extracted with Et2O (10 mL × 6). The organic layer was washed
with brine and dried over Na2SO4. Purification of the product by silica
gel column chromatography (n-hexane:Et2O = 3:1) afforded 12.
3,3,3-Trifluoro-2-hydroxy-2-[1’-(p-tolyl)hydroxymethyl]propanoic acid
methyl ester (12f). 88%; white powder;Diastereomeric mixture (65:35 by 1H
NMR); mp 80-82 °C; IR (neat) 3525, 3070, 2990, 1755, 1525, 1458 cm-1; 1H
NMR (300 MHz) δ 2.33 (s, 3H, major), 2.35 (s, 3H, minor), 2.47 (d, J =
7.5 Hz, 1H, minor), 2.77 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H, major), 3.72 (s, 3H, major),
3.90 (s, 1H, major), 4.00 (s, 3H, minor), 4.12 (s, 1H, minor), 5.17 (d, J
= 7.2 Hz, 1H, minor), 5.23 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H, major), 7.12-7.36 (m, 4H x
2, major and minor mixed); 19F NMR (282 MHz) δ 87.80 (s, 3F, minor),
87.83 (s, 3F, major); EI MS m/z (relative intensity) 200 (M+-78, 11), 120
(100), 92 (32) 77 (14); Anal. Calcd for C12H13F3O4: C, 51.80; H, 4.71.
Found; C, 51.70; H, 4.75.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 65:35 diastereomeric ratio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation and Synthetic Application of a Novel Ketene Silyl Acetal of
Methyl Trifluoropyruvate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
