$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for FeCl3·6H2O-Catalyzed
Mukaiyama Type Reaction. A Schlenk with a Teflon stirring bar was charged
with the corresponding acetal 1 or aldehyde 2 (1 equiv, 0.5 mmol) and
silyl enol ether 3 (1.1 equiv, 0.55 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.29 M) at 0 °C.
Subsequently, FeCl3·6H2O (0.05 equiv, 5 mol %) was added. The reaction
was stirred at room temperature until consumption of the starting
material (monitored by TLC). Next, the reaction was diluted with
dichloromethane (2-3 mL) and filtered over activated aluminum oxide. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the corresponding
products (4 or 5) were isolated by silica gel column chromatography.
5-Hydroxy-2,2-dimethy6-phenylhexan-3-one (5aa). Compound 5aa was prepared
according to the general procedure and was obtained in 88% yield (96.9
mg, 0.44 mmol) as a white dense oil in 1.5 h. Eluents: hexane/ethyl
acetate = 50:1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.49-7.19 (m, 5H), 4.62-4.27
(m, 1H), 3.03-2.50 (m, 4H), 1.21 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
217.3, 138.2, 129.4, 128.5, 126.5, 68.9, 44.2, 42.9, 42.3, 26.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mukaiyama reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM FeCl3·6H2O-Catalyzed Mukaiyama-Aldol Type Reactions of Enolizable
Aldehydes and Acetals
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
