$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reagents: 2-furaldehyde (70 mg, 0.73 mmol), 2-(trimethylsilyloxy)furan 2a
(137 mg, 0.87 mmol), and Bi(OTf)3•4H2O (5.0 mg, 0.0072 mmol). The
reaction was stirred at -78 °C for 0.15 h, then at -45 °C for 0.5 h, and
quenched with sat. aqueous NH4Cl (1 mL). The mixture was then treated
according to the typical procedure. The syn/anti ratio (72:28) was
determined by 1H NMR analysis of the crude product (δ major: 4.80 ppm, δ
minor: 5.03 ppm). The residue was purified by silica gel chromatography
(20% ethyl acetate/hexane) to afford 113 mg (86%) of 3h as a mixture of
unseparable diastereoisomers. Rf = 0.22 (25% ethyl acetate/hexane); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.57 (dd, J = 5.7, 1.6 Hz, 1H (anti)), 7.42 (s,
1H), 7.35 (dd, J = 5.8, 1.5 Hz, 1H (syn)), 6.44 (dd, J = 5.8, 1.6 Hz,
1H), 6.38–6.42 (m, 1H), 6.22 (dd, J = 5.9, 2.0 Hz, 1H (anti)) 6.18 (dd, J
= 5.9, 2.0 Hz, 1H (syn)), 5.32–5.35 (m, 2H), 5.03 (d, J = 4.7 Hz, 1H
(anti)), 4.80 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 1H (syn)), 2.74 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 172.9, 153.5, 153.3, 151.6, 151.3, 143.1, 123.2, 110.9,
108.9, 108.7, 85.2, 84.7, 69.1, 67.9; IR (film): 3382, 1755 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (isomer mix.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
