$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (13) General Procedure for the Vinylogous
Asymmetric Mukaiyama-Type Aldol Reaction. A flame-dried Schlenk flask
under Ar atmosphere was charged with Cu(OTf)2 (18.1 mg, 0.05 mmol) and
aminosulfoximine 1 (0.05 mmol). Then, dry Et2O (2 mL) was added, and the
resulting deep green solution was stirred for 30 min at room temperature.
Subsequently, pyruvate ester 2 (0.5 mmol), vinyl ketene acetal 5 (0.55
mmol), and 2,2,2- trifluoroethanol (0.6 mmol, 44 μL) were added. After
stirring for the indicated period of time, trifluoroacetic acid (0.2 mL)
was added, and the solution was stirred for 30 min. The reaction mixture
was then diluted with Et2O, and a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3
was added slowly. The aqueous layer was extracted three times with Et2O,
and the combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4. The solvent was
removed, and the product was purified by flash chromatography.
(S)-E-5-Hydroxy-5-phenyl-hex-2-enedioc acid 1-tert-butyl ester 6-methyl
ester (6eA): The product was prepared according to the general procedure
(see footnote 13 in text) using methyl benzoylformate (2e, 71 μL, 0.5
mmol) and silyl vinyl ketene acetal 5A (141 mg, 0.55 mmol). It was
obtained as colorless oil in 88% yield (135 mg, 0.44 mmol) after flash
chromatography (pentane/EtOAc: 9/1). [α]D20 = −8.9 (c = 1.2, CHCl3);
1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.45 (s, 9H, tBu), 2.84-2.89 (m, 1H, CH2),
3.03-3.09 (m, 1H, CH2), 3.78 (s, 3H, CH3), 5.83 (d, J = 15.7 Hz, 1H, CH),
6.73- 6.80 (m, 1H, CH), 7.25-7.38 (m, 3H, Ph), 7.55-7.58 (m, 2H, Ph) ppm;
13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 28.2, 42.3, 53.5, 77.9, 80.4, 125.3, 126.9,
128.1, 128.4, 141.0, 140.9, 165.3, 174.4 ppm; MS (70 eV, EI): m/z (%) =
307 (1) [M+H+], 165 (99), 105 (100), 86 (22), 57 (29); IR (film): ν =
3665, 2977, 1713, 1654, 1256, 1157, 919 cm-1 ; elemental analysis (%)
calcd. for C17H22O5 (306.36): C 66.65, H 7.24; found: C 66.58, H 7.17.
The enantiomer ratio was determined by HPLC analysis using a Chiralcel AD
column (flow rate 0.4 mL/min, heptane/iPr-OH: 98/2, λ = 230 nm, 20 °C);
tr = 77.0 min [minor], tr = 90.5 min [major]; 89% ee (93% ee when the
reaction is performed at -78 °C).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, reaction at low temp. gave higher stereoselectivity but
lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Sulfoximines as Ligands in Copper-Catalyzed Asymmetric Vinylogous
Mukaiyama-Type Aldol Reactions
