$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (+)-Methyl(3S)-5-{[tert-Butyl(dimethyl)silyl]oxy}-3-hydroxy-2,2-dimethylpentanoate
(37). To a solution of N-Ts-D-valine (1.36 g, 5.0 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (50
mL) was added dropwise at room temperature a solution of BH3·THF (5 mL, 1
M in THF, 5.0 mmol) over a period of 30 min, and stirring was continued
for 20 min. The reaction was cooled to -78 °C, and a solution of aldehyde
3518 (940 mg, 5.0 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (5 mL) was slowly added followed by
a solution of freshly distilled ketene acetal 36 (960 mg, 5.5 mmol) in
dry CH2Cl2 (5 mL). After being stirred for 4 h at the same temperature,
the reaction mixture was quenched by addition of phosphate buffer (35 mL,
pH = 6.9). The mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 20 mL), and the
combined organic solutions were dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The residue was treated with cold hexane, and the
precipitated N-Ts-D-valine was recovered by filtration (96%). The
solution was again concentrated under reduced pressure and purified by
flash column chromatography (silica gel, elution with hexanes-EtOAc, 5:1)
to obtain 1.25 g (4.3 mmol, 88%) of the β-hydroxy ester 37 as a colorless
oil. Rf 0.39 (hexanes-EtOAc, 5:1, CM: blue);[α]20D +3.0 (c 1.88, CHCl3);
IR (film) 3630 br, 1733, 1472, 1257, 1193, 1138, 1099, cm-1; 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 3.92 (m, 1H), 3.87 (dd,J = 10.0, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 3.80 (m,
1H), 3.68 (s, 3H), 3.37 (d,J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 1.57 (ddd,J = 11.0, 5.5, 1.0
Hz, 2H), 1.19 (s, 3H), 1.15 (s, 3H), 0.88 (s, 9H), 0.06 (s, 6H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 177.8, 76.0, 62.6, 51.8, 47.1, 33.7, 25.9, 21.3, 20.6,
18.2, -5.5; MS (FI) m/e 291 (M+). Anal. Calcd for C14H30O4Si: C, 57.9; H,
10.4. Found: C, 58.26; H, 10.31.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, reaction quenched with buffer
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Syntheses of Epothilones B and D
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mulzer, Johann; Mantoulidis, Andreas; Oehler, Elisabeth
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2000), 65(22), 7456-7467

