$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction. Benzaldehyde (51 0.5 mmol) was added to a
solution of in situ prepared 2a (0.55 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL) at -78 °C
followed by the addition of 1-(trimethylsiloxy)-1-cyclohexene (107 4,
0.55 mmol). The reaction was monitored by TLC analysis and completion was
confirmed after 3.5 h. The whole mixture was poured into 1 N HCl and
extracted with ether. The ethereal extracts were washed with saturated
NaHCO3 and brine, and dried over Na2SO4. The solvents were removed by
evaporation and the residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel (CH2Cl2/hexane = 1:2 to CH2Cl2 as eluant) to give the
corresponding aldol product, 2-(1'-trimethylsiloxybenzy1)-1-cyclohexanone
[12 (R = SiMe3)]8 (121 mg, 0.44 mmol, 87% yield, erythro/threo = 1:3):
2-(1'-trimethylsiloxybenzy1)-1-cyclohexanone [12 (R = SiMe3)]8, yield 121
mg, 0.44 mmol, 87% 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) erythro isomer: δ 7.39-7.15
(5H, m, Ph), 5.54 (1H, d, J= 5.2 Hz, O-CH), 2.60-1.15 (9H, m, CH and
CH2), 0.21 (9H, s, Si(CH3)3); threo isomer: 7.40-7.20 (5H, m, Ph), 5.28
(1H, d, J= 8.1 Hz, O-CH), 2.80-1.15 (9H, m, CH and CH2), 0.20 (9H, s,
Si(CH3)3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 1:3 erythro:threo, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, in-situ
generated reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM (2,7-Disubstituted-1,8-biphenylenedioxy)bis(dimethylaluminum) as
