$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure B; Aldol reaction between 2.2.2-trifluoroacetophenone dm) and
methyl trimethvlsilvl dimethvlketene acetal (2): To 2, 2,
2-Trifluoroacetophenone (0.53 g, 3.0 mmol) in a dry flask under N2 were
added THF (anhydrous, 15 mL), methyl trimethylsilyl dimethylketene acetal
(0.66 g, 3.60 mmol based on 95% purity) and carbene 5 (5 mg, 0.014 mmol).
The mixture was stirred at 23 °C for 3 h. HC1 aq solution (1 N, 3 mL) was
added and most of the solvent was evaporated under vacuum. Methanol (15
mL) and HC1 aq solution (1 N, 3 mL) was added and the solution was
stirred at 23 °C for 10 days. Saturated NaHCO3 solution (3 mL) and water
(3 mL) were added and most of the solvent was evaporated under vacuum.
Dichloromethane (50 mL) was added and the aqueous layer was extracted
with dichloromethane (50 mL). Organic layers were combined and solvents
were removed under vacuum to give the crude residue, which was purified
by silica gel flash chromatography (10% ethyl acetate/hexanes) to give
pure product 6m as a colorless oil (0.71 g, 87% yield). 1H NMR (CDC13,
400 MHz) δ 7.70 (m, 2H), 7.38 (m, 3H), 5.76 (s, 1H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 1.35
(s, 3H), 1.08 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDC13, 100 MHz) δ 178.2, 133.9, 128.7,
127.9, 127.7, 126.1 (q, J C-F = 286 Hz), 80.5 (q, J C-F = 26 Hz), 53.2,
46.8, 23.8, 20.5. HRMS: calcd for [M+H]+ C13H16F3O3, m/z 277.1046, found:
m/z 277.1042. IR (cm-1): 2958, 1699, 1474, 1451, 1437, 1287, 1267, 1195,
1150, 1069, 973, 937, 918, 763, 729, 705, 634, 540, 499.
