$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure of Mukaiyama aldol reaction
Aldehyde (2, 2 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (8 mL), and the solution was
cooled to -30 °C. Then TiCl4 (2 mL, 1.0 M in CH2Cl2) was added slowly
under N2 atmosphere. After 15 min, a solution of silyl enol ether (1, 2
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (4 mL) was added to the mixture dropwise and the mixture
was allowed to react under -30 °C for 1.5 h. After hydrolysis with 5 %
K2CO3 at -30 °C and warm-up, the organic layer was separated and the
aqueous layer was extracted with ether (8 mL× 3). The combined organic
layers were washed with saturated NaCl aqueous (20 mL× 3) and dried over
with Na2SO4. After concentration, product 3 was isolated by flash column
chromatography on silica gel using hexane/Et2O mixture as eluent.
2-(cyclohexyl(hydroxy)methyl)2-fluoro-1-phenylpentan-1-one (3m) syn
isomer: colorless oil; Yield 87%, drc 5.0:1 For the syn isomer: 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.01(d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.57(t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H),
7.45(t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 3.85(dd, J = 25.2, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 2.22-1.95(m,
3H), 1.90-1.47(m, 7H), 1.34-1.05(m, 6H), 0.90(t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H); 13C
NMR(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 202.2(d, JCF= 25.0 Hz), 136.5(d, JCF= 4.0 Hz),
133.1, 129.6(d, JCF= 9.1 Hz), 128.4(d, JCF= 1.5 Hz), 107.8(d, JCF= 194.4
Hz), 78.6(d, JCF= 20.6 Hz), 40.5, 38.3(d, JCF= 22.6 Hz), 31.5(d, JCF= 1.0
Hz), 27.0(d, JCF= 4.0 Hz), 26.4, 26.0(d, JCF= 8.5 Hz), 17.0(d, JCF= 5.0
Hz), 14.3; 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3) δ -172.9(m); IR (neat) ν: 3504(s),
3059(w), 2926(s), 2853(s), 1671(s), 1597(m), 1577(w), 1448(m), 1386(m),
1266(m), 1236(m), 1186(w), 1088(w), 1017(m), 838(w), 756(w), 690(m),
651(m) cm-1; MS (ESI) m/z: 337.1 (M+ COOH-); HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C18H25FO2 (M+Na+) 315.1731, found 315.1738.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, 83:17 syn:anti
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
