$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Desilylation of
Mukaiyama Aldol Compounds. To a mixture of 10 (without purification, 1.0
mmol) in MeOH (5 mL) and THF (2-5 mL) was added 12% HCl(aq) (2.1 mL, 7
mmol), and then the resulting mixture was stirred for an additional 6 h
at 30 °C. After evaporation of most of the MeOH and THF, the resulting
residue was extracted with Et2O (10 mL × 6). The organic layer was washed
with brine and dried over Na2SO4. Purification of the product by silica
gel column chromatography (n-hexane:Et2O = 3:1) afforded 12.
3,3,3-Trifluoro-2-hydroxy-2-[(4-methoxyphenyl)hydroxymethyl]propanoic
acid methyl ester (12a). 87%; oily solid;Diastereomeric mixture (52:48 by
1H NMR); mp 48-49 °C ; IR (neat) 3512, 3016, 2968, 2848, 1754, 1766,
1616, 1588, 1516, 1444, 1480, 1458 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz) δ 2.63 (s, J =
7.8 Hz, 1H, minor), 2.91 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H, major), 3.70 (s, 3H, major),
3.78 (s, 3H, major), 3.80 (s, 3H, minor), 3.97 (s, 3H, minor), 3.99 (s,
1H, major), 4.18 (s, 1H, minor), 5.15 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H, minor), 5.20
(s, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, major), 6.84 (dd, J = 1.8 Hz, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H, major),
6.88 (dd, J = 1.8 Hz, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H, minor), 7.24 (dd, J = 1.8 Hz, J =
6.6 Hz, 2H, major), 7.38 (d, J = 1.8 Hz, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H, minor); 19F NMR
(282 MHz) δ 87.81 (s, 3F, minor), 87.82 (s, 3F, major); EI MS m/z
(relative intensity) 294 (M+, trace), 137 (100), 109 (33), 94 (23); 77
