$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A typical procedure for Mukaiyama aldol
reaction. To a suspension of PMI Sc(OTf)3 (135 mg, 0.025 mmol, 5 mol%) in
CH2Cl2 (3.0 mL) were added a solution of benzaldehyde (53 mg, 0.50 mmol)
in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL) and a solution of the ketene silyl acetal derived from
methyl isobutyrate (113 mg, 0.65 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL) at 0 °C under
Ar. The mixture was stirred for 10 min at the same temperature and
stirred for 3 h at room temperature. After filtration and washing
(CH2Cl2, hexane), the filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure.
The divided crude compounds (see: ICP analysis section) were treated with
1N HCl/THF (1/10) at room temperature to hydrolyze the silyl ether. After
usual work up, the crude compounds were purified by PTLC to give methyl
3-hydroxy-2,2-dimethyl-3-phenylpropionate (48 mg, 46% (corrected yield;
92%)). PMI Sc(OTf)3 was recovered quantitatively (> 97%) and reused, the
2nd run; 96%, the 3rd run; 94%. In the 2nd and 3rd run, all recovered
crude compounds after the reaction were treated to determine the yield of
the desired compound. Methyl 3-hydroxy-2,2-dimethyl-3-phenylpropionate:3
White powder; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ = 1.10 (s, 3H), 1.14 (s, 3H), 3.03 (br s,
1H), 3.70 (s, 3H), 4.88 (s, 1H), 7.22–7.33 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ =
19.0, 22.9, 47.7, 52.0, 78.6, 127, 6, 127.7, 139.9, 178.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Polymer-Micelle Incarcerated Scandium as a Polymer-Supported Catalyst for
High-Throughput Organic Synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Takeuchi, Masahiro; Akiyama, Ryo; Kobayashi, Shu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2005), 127(38), 13096-13097

