$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of aldehyde (0.8 mmol) in
propionitrile (0.32 mL) was added over 10 min to a mixed solution of the
silyl enol ether (0.96 mmol) and 2d (0.08 mmol) in propionitrile (0.65
mL). 3-Hydroxy-2-methyl-1-phenyl-4-hexen-1-one (Table 3), yield 85%. 1H
NMR, 13C NMR, and IR spectroscopic data are in agreement with those
reported in the literature.1c The syn/anti ratio was determined by 1H NMR
spectroscopy: 1H NMR (CDCl3 , 300 MHz) δ 1.18 (d, J=7.3 Hz, 3H, CHCH3
(anti isomer)), 1.27 (d, J=7.3 Hz, 3H, CHCH3 (syn isomer)), 2.70 (brd,
J=5.7 Hz, 1H, OH (anti isomer)), 2.99 (brs, 1H, OH (syn isomer)), 4.35
(q, J=7.2 Hz, 1H, CHOH (anti isomer)), 4.50-4.57 (m, J=5.0 Hz, 1H, CHOH
(syn isomer)); The enantiomeric ratios were determined by HPLC analysis
(two linear Daicel OD-H columns with hexane-i-PrOH=20:1, flow rato. 6
ml/min): tR=24. 3 (syn, major enantiomer (2R, 3S)), 28.7 (syn, minor
enantiomer (2S, 3R)), 33.1 (anti, one enantiomer), 33.6 (anti, another
enantiomer) min; The absolute configuration of the syn isomer was
determined by the comparison of optical rotation values with data in the
literature:1c [α]D28.1=.-21.9 (c=1.3, CHCl3).
