$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Condensation Reaction Between 2,4-Bis(silyloxy)penta-1,3-diene (2-Si) and
syn-Aldehyde 15. To a solution of the aldehyde 15 (71.1 mg, 0.29 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (2 mL) at -78°C was added BF3OEt2 (107 L, 0.87 mmol, 3.0 equiv).
After 10 min at -78°C, bis(silyl) enol ether 2-Si (242 L, 0.87 mmol, 3.0
equiv) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred at -78°C for 10
min, and then quenched with sat. aq NaHCO3 solution (10 mL) and diluted
with Et2O (10 mL). The layers were separated and the aqueous phase was
extracted with Et2O (3 10 mL). The combined organic layers were washed
with brine, dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash-chromatography on silica gel (30:70 Et2O-petroleum
ether) afforded the aldol 16 as a 84:16 mixture of syn-and
anti-diastereomers.
(6R*,7S*,8S*)-8-tert-(Butyldimethylsilyloxy)-6-hydroxy-7,9-dimethyldecan-2,4-dione
(syn-16): Colorless oil, yield 85.2 mg, 85%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
(3:1 mixture of regiomeric enols) = 0.04-0.12 [m, 6 H, Si(CH3)2],
0.83-1.00 [m, 18 H, SiC(CH3)3, CH3-7, CH(CH3)2], 1.63-1.90 (m, 2 H, H-7,
H-9), 2.05 (2 s, 3 H, H3- 1), 2.22-2.41 (m, 1 H, H-5), 2.46 (d, J = 6.2
Hz, 1 H, OH), 2.56- 2.68 (m, 1 H, H-5), 3.45-3.64 (m, 0.75 H, H-8), 3.71
(dd, J = 5.7, 2.1 Hz, 0.25 H, H-8), 3.95-4.12 (m, 0.75 H, H-6), 4.18
(ddd, J = 8.6, 6.1, 2.7 Hz, 0.25 H, H-6), 5.53 (s, 0.75 H, H-3), 5.57 (s,
0.25 H, H-3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama condensation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 2-acetonyl-2,4-di(hydroxy)tetrahydropyrans versus γ-pyrones: a
chemodivergent issue for the condensation of acetylacetone dianion
equivalents with α,β-disubstituted β-hydroxyaldehydes leading to
potential new synthons for spiroketals
