$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the aldol reaction To a
stirred solution of the aldehyde 1c (130 mg, 236 μmol) in freshly
distilled CH2Cl2 (5 mL) cooled to -60 °C was added the BF3.OEt2 (90 μL,
710 μmol) with a syringe. After 5 min 7 (102 μL, 472 μmol) was added and
the mixture stirred at -60 °C for 18h. The reaction was quenched with
saturated NaHCO3 (5 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x10 mL). The combined
organic phases were dried (MgSO4), filtered and evaporated to give a
colorless oil. The diastereomeric ratio was determined by 1H NMR on the
crude reaction mixture. Flash chromatography of the residue
(pentane:EtOAc 20:1) yielded 3b (141 mg, 92%) as a colorless oil.
N-Benzyl-N-((1S*,2R*)-2-hydroxy-1-isopropyl-5,5-dimethyl-4-oxo-hexyl)-4-methylbenzenesulfonamide
(9) 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.68 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.46 (d, J = 7.0
Hz, 2H), 7.35-7.21 (m, 5H), 4.61 (d, 15.4 Hz, 1H), 4.36 (d, 15.4 Hz, 1H),
4.01 (m, 1H), 3.43 (m, 1H), 3.26 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 2.53 (m, 2H), 2.42
(s, 3H), 1.91 (m, 1H), 1.04 (s, 9H), 0.74 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 217.5, 143.2, 138.2, 137.6, 129.6, 129.1, 128.4,
127.7, 127.3, 69.2, 44.2, 41.7, 29.3, 26.3, 22.3, 21.5, 20.2; IR (neat)
3400, 2970, 1690, 1160 cm-1; HRMS (FAB+) calcd for C25H36NO4S (M+H):
446.2365, found: 446.2359.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
