$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7. A general procedure for 4b·L2-catalyzed Mukaiyama aldol reaction with
ketones: Freshly distilled THF (5 mL) was injected at room temperature
under nitrogen into pyrex Schrenk tube containing sodium phenoxide (5b)
(2.9 mg, 0.025 mmol) and 1,2-bis(diphenylphosphoryl)benzene (L) (23.9 mg,
0.050 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 10 min at that temperature, and
then this colorless solution was cooled to –78 °C and stirred for 5 min
at that temperature. methyl
2-methyl-2-(9-(trimethylsilyloxy)-9H-fluoren-9-yl)propanoate (3l). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.32 (s, 9H), 1.17 (s, 6H), 3.57 (s, 3H), 7.22 (td, J
= 7.2, 1.2 Hz, 2H), 7.34 (td, J = 7.5, 1.2 Hz, 2H), 7.41 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
2H), 7.57 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.2, 21.3, 51.0,
51.3, 87.1, 119.5, 125.6, 126.7, 128.8, 140.4, 147.6, 176.0. IR(film)
2950, 1730, 1449, 1263, 1250, 1145, 1078 cm-1. HRMS(FAB+) calcd for
C21H26NaO3Si [M+Na]+ 377.1549, found 377.1544.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Sodium Phenoxide-Phosphine Oxides as Extremely Active Lewis Base
Catalysts for the Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction with Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hatano, Manabu; Takagi, Eri; Ishihara, Kazuaki
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(22), 4527-4530

